* ideal_opamp_rr_dual.lib
* Behavioral rail-to-rail dual op-amp model
* (MCP6002, MCP6007, NCS20072DTB)
*
* Output is clamped within 50 mV of the supply rails,
* modelling the near-rail output swing of R2R output-stage devices.
*
* Pin order:  in1m in1p vcc vee out1 in2p in2m out2
*   (same as ideal_opamp_dual.lib — drop-in replacement)
*
* KiCad Sim.Pins for 8-pin dual op-amp:
*   Sim.Pins = "2 3 8 4 1 5 6 7"

.subckt IDEAL_OPAMP_RR_DUAL in1m in1p vcc vee out1 in2p in2m out2
* High input impedance
Rin1 in1p in1m 1G
Rin2 in2p in2m 1G
* Behavioral output: gain 100k, output clamped to within 50 mV of rails
B1 out1 0 V = max(V(vee)+0.05, min(V(vcc)-0.05, 100000*(V(in1p)-V(in1m))))
B2 out2 0 V = max(V(vee)+0.05, min(V(vcc)-0.05, 100000*(V(in2p)-V(in2m))))
.ends IDEAL_OPAMP_RR_DUAL
